;; bsv-low #731: the D1 budget tier's egress SEAL (macOS sandbox-exec). The tier's `wrangler dev` workers may reach
;; the loopback only; a subrequest to any other address fails closed (the worker sees a transport fault, the same
;; "could not look" a courier outage gives), so no cell can pass or fail on what mainnet answered. DNS still
;; resolves (a unix socket), so the attempt is still logged and `egress_guard.mjs` reds on it.
(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny network-outbound (remote ip "*:*"))
(allow network-outbound (remote ip "localhost:*"))
